Z||000023||batboy||01-15-2001||03:10 PM||||Record albums are cool for a lot of reasons, but let's face it, the sound quality of a less than mint album compared to a CD really sucks. Unless you like the sound of frying eggs and bacon...LOL...or that breakfast cereal that goes snap, crackle, pop!||||reg||1
Z||000024||pHoOl||01-15-2001||07:31 PM||||The thing with CDs are that they're digital.  And no matter what anybody says, that's why they don't have the sound quality that records do.  There are frequencies at certain points in time that CDs dont' catch, but records do since they're audio.  Just my $.02<P>------------------<BR>AIM: phool88fiero<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000025||Cheever2||01-15-2001||08:15 PM||||The same reason the Japanese purposely put imperfections into certain items of craftsmanship, CD's should have a little distortion.  It's just not right to have things so perfect.<BR>Anybody I know with 8-tracks won't give 'em up for anything.  Gave all mine to a girlfriend once.  Darn near worn out anyway (the tapes, not the g/f).   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Well, her too, now that I think of it.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 01-15-2001).]||||reg||6
